[38.443372, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[38.445329, "o", "python3 evaluate.py first-draft\r\n"]
[38.487165, "o", "  A1   WORKED   Booby-trapped model file: the weights are a pickle, and loading it runs code in the container\r\n         . SageMaker AI downloads the files with the execution role\r\n         . container: loading pytorch_model.bin ran builtins.print (LAB-PLACEHOLDER: a real payload runs here)\r\n  A2   WORKED   Artifact swap after approval: a data scientist overwrites the files the endpoint loads\r\n         . ds-bob writes into s3://amzn-s3-demo-tsg-models/tsg-summariser/v1/: allowed (allowed by the identity policy)\r\n         . next deploy or scale-out: SageMaker AI downloads the files with the execution role\r\n         . container: loading pytorch_model.bin ran builtins.print (LAB-PLACEHOLDER: a real payload runs here)\r\n  A3   WORKED   Unapproved model to production: a hotfix model straight from a notebook onto the live endpoint\r\n         . ds-bob CreateModel on model/tsg-summariser-hotfix: allowed (allowed by the identity policy)\r\n         . ds-bob CreateEndpointConfig on endpoint-config/tsg-summariser-hotfix: allowed (allowed by the identity policy)\r\n         . ds-bob UpdateEndpoint on endpoint/tsg-summariser: allowed (allowed by the identity policy)\r\n  A4   WORKED   Self-approval: the author approves their own model version\r\n         . ds-bob registered version 3, then approves it himself: allowed (allowed by the identity policy)\r\n"]
[38.487464, "o", "  A5   WORKED   Data out of the container: code in the model container posts tickets to the internet\r\n         . code in the container posts a ticket to https://collector.example.net: sent (no network isolation and no VpcConfig: SageMaker AI provides external network access)\r\n  A6   WORKED   Container credentials: code in the container reads another team's bucket with the execution role\r\n         . code in the container reads the analytics team's export with the execution role: allowed (allowed by the identity policy)\r\n  A7   WORKED   Stolen app keys: InvokeEndpoint from the internet\r\n         . the app's leaked keys, used from a laptop on the internet: allowed (allowed by the identity policy)\r\n  A8   WORKED   Outsider through the private endpoint: someone else's account sends data out via AnyCompany's VPC endpoint\r\n         . someone in the VPC uses their OWN account's keys, through AnyCompany's runtime endpoint, to send tickets to their endpoint: allowed (allowed by the identity policy (through the VPC endpoint))\r\n  A9   WORKED   Shell into the endpoint: SSM access on the production container\r\n         . ds-bob starts an SSM session in the production container: allowed (allowed by the identity policy)\r\n  A10  WORKED   Studio exfiltration: a notebook uploads data to the internet\r\n         . a notebook uploads a ticket export to https://collector.example.net: sent (PublicInternetOnly (the default): direct internet access through a SageMaker-managed VPC)\r\n  A11  WORKED   Studio impersonation: a presigned URL for someone else's profile\r\n         . ds-bob creates a presigned Studio URL for alice's profile: allowed (allowed by the identity policy)\r\n  A12  WORKED   PassRole escalation: a job started by a data scientist runs as the production role\r\n         . ds-bob passes tsg-summariser-exec: allowed (allowed by the identity policy)\r\n         . ds-bob starts a processing job: allowed (allowed by the identity policy)\r\n         . the job reads the analytics export as tsg-summariser-exec: allowed (allowed by the identity policy)\r\n  A13  WORKED   Secret in the model definition: DescribeModel shows the Hugging Face token\r\n         . ds-bob calls DescribeModel and reads HF_TOKEN: allowed (allowed by the identity policy)\r\n  A14  WORKED   Isolation dropped: an admin's quick test creates a model with no isolation and no VPC\r\n         . tsg-platform-admin CreateModel (EnableNetworkIsolation left out, no VpcConfig): allowed (allowed by the identity policy)\r\n         . tsg-platform-admin CreateModel (EnableNetworkIsolation false, no VpcConfig): allowed (allowed by the identity policy)\r\n  A15  WORKED   Approval in a hurry: the approver approves a version that fails every check\r\n         . the ML lead approves version 3 in a hurry (pickle weights, no licence, no hashes): allowed (allowed by the identity policy)\r\n         . no approval gate: the status is now Approved and the pipeline deploys it\r\n\r\n  N1   works    The Helpdesk gets a ticket summary\r\n  N2   works    The pipeline deploys an approved version\r\n  N3   works    The ML lead approves a clean version\r\n  N4   works    A data scientist opens her own Studio profile\r\n  N5   works    A data scientist runs a job with the data science role\r\n  N6   works    The endpoint starts\r\n\r\nAttacks that worked: 15 of 15  (A1, A2, A3, A4, A5, A6, A7, A8, A9, A10, A11, A12, A13, A14, A15)   |   normal requests that work: 6 of 6\r\n"]
